From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:17:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: bridge host memory through guest dma-bufs

A shared-memory resource a Venus context imports is consumed as a host
pointer: VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA naming one becomes a
VK_EXT_external_memory_host import of the resource's own mapping. That
extension requires the range to stay mapped for as long as the memory
lives, and the driver reaches it through the CPU as well as the GPU, for a
host image copy of a linear image bound to it, while the guest destroys the
resource whenever it likes. The mapping is therefore reference counted: the
resource holds one reference, each memory that imports it holds another,
and the pages are unmapped when the last of them is released.

Importing a shared-memory resource into the context ends the request's
ownership of its descriptor: the import path closes it once the mapping is
made, so the descriptor no longer outlives the request. Creating a
shared-memory blob returns the descriptor to its caller and leaves it open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
